*  OPSYN of a USED operator is ERROR 156 (manual p.116: "OPSYN first arg is not correct operator name";
*  p.271 error list).  SPITBOL forbids redefining + - * / ** etc. -- and says so explicitly so that the
*  compiler MAY assume their identity.  SCRIP must raise 156 here, not silently accept.
        DEFINE('PLUS(a,b)')                                 :(p_end)
PLUS    PLUS           =   a + b                            :(RETURN)
p_end
        OPSYN('+', 'PLUS', 2)
        OUTPUT         =   1 + 2
END
